;. /cartography_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition cartography
  ;= Maintain an evidence cartography

    Create and publish Web evidence, then Cited assertions, before publishing
    this parent. The parent captures both child definitions. Later edits to a
    child do not silently replace the procedure retained by this publication.

    Attach this flow from Nenex using the ordinary maintenance controls. Bind
    urls, subject and projection, choose the Nenex writer and an existing native
    Codex provider, and select a new destination page. HTTP tasks select their
    existing provider; judgment and prose use the chosen shared provider.
    Inspect the occurrence's cells, native attempts, context overlays and holes.

    Change a URL record's revision to request new evidence. A changed result
    resumes dependent work, while older captures and attempts remain. A missing
    source cannot become current evidence. Edited generated prose is protected
    by the existing document writer. Search, source discovery and identity
    merging are not performed by this procedure.

    ;@ /flow/input urls
    ;= Named URL records

    ;@ /flow/input subject
    ;= Explicit subject reference and question

    ;@ /flow/input projection
    ;= Selected raw native projection record

    ;@ /flow/invoke sources ;/0x11/app/nenex/w/web_evidence_flow/flows/web_evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind urls urls
    ;= Capture and structure evidence using the reusable child

    ;@ /flow/invoke reviewed ;/0x11/app/nenex/w/cited_assertions_flow/flows/cited_assertions
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;@ /flow/bind subject subject
    ;@ /flow/bind projection projection
    ;= Propose, validate, project and judge cited assertions

    ;@ /flow/step concepts ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/revise
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources reviewed
    ;= Author the explanation through the shared revision hand

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind pages concepts
    ;@ /flow/bind sources reviewed
    ;= Publish a concept and compact source provenance

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= Guarded document publication

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;@ /flow/uses review
    ;= Evidence cartography
      Explain the explicit subject using only the reviewed, source-qualified
      assertions. Include exact source references and quotations where useful.
      Distinguish quoted evidence from acceptance judgments and interpretation.
      Describe the selected evidence scope and its limits. Do not claim complete
      discovery, merge entities by name, invent facts or reproduce source files.
      If the supplied evidence cannot support an explanation, return empty
      source with the reason; the existing revision hole must remain unresolved.
